 html←PrepareHtmlPageForTagList data;tags;letters;letter;bool
⍝ Returns the page listing all tags as an alphabetical index, with a filter.
⍝ `data` comes from `Reg.ListTags`: per row a tag and the number of packages carrying it. The
⍝ numbers are not shown: this page is for finding a tag, and a tag leads to the list of packages
⍝ filtered by it, which says how many there are.
⍝ Tags that do not start with a letter are listed under "#".
⍝ The filter is done by the script Assets/JS/tag-list.js. Without JavaScript the index is still
⍝ complete, only without the filter: it is written with `hidden` set, and the script shows it.
 html←(⍬'Tags' '/tags')HtmlHeader⊂'<script src="/Assets/JS/tag-list.js" defer></script>'
 html,←⊂'<div class="page-head">'
 html,←⊂'<h2>Tags</h2>'
 html,←⊂'<div class="list-tools" id="tag-tools" hidden>'
 html,←⊂'<label class="filter" for="tag-filter"><span class="sr-only">Filter the tags</span><input type="search" id="tag-filter" placeholder="Filter tags…" autocomplete="off"><kbd title="Press / to jump into the filter">/</kbd></label>'
 html,←⊂'</div>'
 html,←⊂'</div>'
 tags←∪⎕C A.DLB A.DTB data[;1]                    ⍝ Blanks around a tag are no part of it, nor is the case
 tags←(0<≢¨tags)/tags
 tags←tags[⍋tags]
 letters←{(⊃⍵)∊⎕C ⎕A:1 ⎕C⊃⍵ ⋄ '#'}¨tags
 html,←⊂'<div class="tag-index" id="tag-index">'
 :For letter :In ∪letters
     bool←letters=letter
     html,←⊂'<section class="tag-letter">'
     html,←⊂'<h3>',letter,'</h3>'
     html,←⊂'<ul>'
     html,←{'<li><a href="',Reg.VersionOf_REST,'/packages?tag=',(EscapeAttributeValue ⍵),'">',(EscapeSpecialChars ⍵),'</a></li>'}¨bool/tags
     html,←⊂'</ul>'
     html,←⊂'</section>'
 :EndFor
 html,←⊂'</div>'
 html,←⊂'<p class="no-match" id="tag-none" hidden>No tag contains what you typed.</p>'
 html,←⊆GetFooter
 html,←⊂'</body>'
 html,←⊂'</html>'
⍝Done
